<% content_for :title, "How we protect your details — Nyika Village Registry" %>

<section class="bg-village text-white">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-14">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">How we protect your details</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-white/85">
      A register is only worth having if people trust it. These are the rules it
      is built on, not promises added afterwards.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-14">
  <div class="grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <article class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
      <h2 class="font-bold text-village">You agree to each use separately</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-slate-700">
        There is no single box that signs your family up to everything. You agree
        to each of these on its own, and you can withdraw any of them later.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-700">
        <%# Drawn from the same list the consent forms use, so the wording here
            and the wording someone actually agrees to cannot drift apart. %>
        <% ConsentRecord::PURPOSE_DESCRIPTIONS.each do |purpose, description| %>
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-gold"></span>
            <span><strong><%= purpose.humanize %>.</strong> <%= description %></span>
          </li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
      <h2 class="font-bold text-village">What we deliberately do not ask for</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-slate-700">
        The less we hold, the less can go wrong. We do not record:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-700">
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-slate-400"></span>National ID numbers, or copies of identity documents</li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-slate-400"></span>Health details or income</li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-slate-400"></span>Claims about who owns which land</li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-slate-400"></span>Dates of birth — an age band is enough</li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-slate-400"></span>Where exactly your homestead sits — a description in words is enough</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
      <h2 class="font-bold text-village">Nothing changes quietly</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-slate-700">
        Every change records who made it, when, and why. Records are never
        deleted — if a household leaves, the record is closed, not erased, so the
        history stays checkable. You can ask to see everything held about you and
        have anything wrong corrected.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
      <h2 class="font-bold text-village">Not everyone sees everything</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-slate-700">
        Different people at the village office can see different things. Whoever
        registers households cannot see who has asked for welfare support, and
        whoever runs support cases cannot see who contributed to a collection.
        Nobody should be able to link the two.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
      <h2 class="font-bold text-village">Money is checked, not held</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-slate-700">
        The register never holds your money. You pay to an approved account or an
        authorised collector, and the office records the receipt. Whoever takes a
        payment is never the person who confirms it arrived.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
      <h2 class="font-bold text-village">Never sold, never political</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-slate-700">
        Your details are not sold to anyone. An approved partner may contact you
        only if you have specifically agreed to that. The register is not used for
        political fundraising, and support you receive is never linked to who you
        support.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-12 rounded-2xl border border-rule bg-white p-8">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-village">If something is wrong</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-slate-700">
      Speak to the village office. You can see what is recorded about your
      household, correct it, withdraw an agreement, or ask for a new link if
      someone else has seen yours.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
